  "description": "A Playful, capable, and versatile short travel trail bike that might just be the only mountain bike you’ll ever need. The HB912 blends modern trail geometry with Hope’s proven engineering and attention to detail. Whether you’re flowing through singletrack, taking on technical terrain, or heading out for big days in the hills, the HB912 is built to do it all. A 29er carbon fibre frame built for speed, efficiency, and confidence across varied terrain. With 120mm of rear travel matched to a 130mm fork, the HB912 hits the sweet spot between lively climbing performance and confident descending capability. An adjustable 65–66° head angle allows riders to tune the bike’s handling to suit their riding style and terrain, while the steep 77.5° seat tube angle keeps pedalling efficient and comfortable. Similar to all our other models, the complete frame is produced in house at our Barnoldswick factory, and comes in three sizes. The build is completed with a SRAM Transmission drivetrain, RockShox suspension, and a full Hope finishing kit: delivering reliability, precision, and unmistakable Hope quality throughout.",
